<li><strong>Smoke and soot.</strong> Smoke from a nearby fire can leave residue on exterior surfaces, HVAC systems, and contents. See <a href="/services/smoke-damage-claims/">smoke damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Business interruption.</strong> Local businesses that depend on plant activity may face income losses when facilities shut down after a storm. Whether business income coverage applies depends on the cause and the policy. See <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claims</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Port Neches homes and buildings</h2>
<p>Port Neches housing is mostly single-family homes, many of them older, on slabs or piers and beams, with composition shingle roofs and brick veneer, wood, vinyl, or fiber-cement siding. Commercial buildings range from small retail and office buildings to metal shops and warehouses with low-slope or metal roofs. In this humid climate, any water that gets into walls, attics, or crawlspaces can lead to mold quickly, so fast drying and good documentation are essential.</p>

